From 5d428f62f0a3171a74e64b43ec37c34dca1be860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unrent <jimmyschade@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:11:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] partykit: let the Unreal kart host host rooms in production

The Unreal Engine kart host connects with Unreal's libwebsockets client, which on Windows always
sends Origin: http://<server host>, so against production it presents http://party.movecade.com
and was refused as an unlisted, non-https origin.

Admit exactly that origin (NATIVE_HOST_ORIGINS) in production and exempt it, by value, from the
https-only check. No browser page can present it, and a non-browser client could already send any
Origin, so nothing new opens to websites; every other plain-http origin is still refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
